Usage:
  commons verify [--rerun] [--exec-policy <file>] [--policy <file>] <digest|id>
      [--json]

check a blob or a statement from the statements held; exit per the exit table

Statement-only by default: verify reads the statements this store holds and runs
nothing. With --rerun (a blob only) and --exec-policy <file>, the reader re-runs
the derivation under its own execution policy and the re-run's token replaces
the derivation cause; without a policy the re-run is unchecked and nothing runs.

Exit 0 checked and passed, 1 a completed comparison disagreed, 3 could not
check, 4 nothing to re-run, 5 environment mismatch.

Options:
  --rerun               re-run the blob's derivation under --exec-policy and
                        compare it with the pin (a blob only); never the default
  --exec-policy <file>  the reader's execution policy file (format
                        rc-exec-policy/0, provisional); only applies alongside
                        --rerun
  --policy <file>       the reader policy (reader-policy-v1) to answer under
                        (default: $COMMONS_POLICY; none when neither is set;
                        nothing is read implicitly; format:
                        docs/READER-POLICY.md)

Examples:
  commons verify --store store <digest>
